    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I see math as a tool that connects physics and computer science, which are my favorite subjects. It helps me understand patterns, even if I don't always enjoy the calculations. I use it to solve problems in coding and game strategies, though I often feel more comfortable with hands-on tasks than abstract theory.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Sometimes, yes. When I try to focus on complex formulas or proofs, I feel a tightness in my chest, especially if I can't see how it applies to real life. My low conscientiousness and moderate extraversion make structured math tasks feel isolating and overwhelming, even though I'm not generally neurotic.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I've used AI tools like chatbots to check solutions and explain steps in physics-related math. It helped when I was stuck, but I often got confused by overly technical explanations. I prefer learning through games or climbing, so AI felt useful but not natural — more like a shortcut than a teacher.",
